      "message": "Mulin and Michal,\nAfter enabling fan and tach in zephyr I see below if fan is in rpm mode\n\nZephyr EC: \n22-04-05 15:23:20.815 ec:~$ faninfo\n22-04-05 15:23:23.104 Actual:    0 rpm\n22-04-05 15:23:23.107 Target:    0 rpm\n22-04-05 15:23:23.109 Duty:   0%\n22-04-05 15:23:23.109 Status: 0 (not spinning)\n22-04-05 15:23:23.112 Mode:   rpm\n22-04-05 15:23:23.113 Auto:   yes\n22-04-05 15:23:23.113 Enable: yes\n22-04-05 15:23:23.114 Power:  yes\n\nIf running fan in duty mode by setting pwm duty manually \"fanduty 50\" through EC command I see below faninfo :\n\n22-04-06 11:37:55.806 ec:~$ faninfo\n22-04-06 11:37:57.975 Actual: 3932 rpm\n22-04-06 11:37:57.977 Target:    0 rpm\n22-04-06 11:37:57.978 Duty:   50%\n22-04-06 11:37:57.979 Status: 2 (locked)\n22-04-06 11:37:57.981 Mode:   duty\n22-04-06 11:37:57.982 Auto:   no\n22-04-06 11:37:57.983 Enable: yes\n22-04-06 11:37:57.984 Power:  yes\n\n\nLegacy EC:\n22-04-06 11:27:51.027 \u003e faninfo\n22-04-06 11:27:53.015 Actual: 3996 rpm\n22-04-06 11:27:53.018 Target: 4131 rpm\n22-04-06 11:27:53.019 Duty:   22%\n22-04-06 11:27:53.020 Status: 2 (locked)\n22-04-06 11:27:53.037 Mode:   rpm\n22-04-06 11:27:53.039 Auto:   yes\n22-04-06 11:27:53.040 Enable: yes\n22-04-06 11:27:53.041 Power:  yes\n\nLegacy EC uses fan configuration as:\n/* PWM configuration */\nconst struct pwm_t pwm_channels[] \u003d {\n        [PWM_CH_FAN] \u003d {\n                .channel \u003d PWN_FAN_CHANNEL,\n                .flags \u003d 0,\n                .freq \u003d 30000,\n        },\n};\nBUILD_ASSERT(ARRAY_SIZE(pwm_channels) \u003d\u003d PWM_CH_COUNT);\n\nconst struct mft_t mft_channels[] \u003d {\n        [MFT_CH_0] \u003d {\n                .module \u003d NPCX_MFT_MODULE_2,\n                .clk_src \u003d TCKC_LFCLK,\n                .pwm_id \u003d PWM_CH_FAN,\n        },\n};\n\n\n\nCan you see if we are missing anything or doing wrong configuring  for tach/fan in dts file?",
